  m_text: "A normal map stores a direction for each pixel. The shader uses it instead of the mesh's own normals when it computes the light.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> Move the Point Light around the spheres. Does the outline of the right sphere become bumpy?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Select Point Light - move me and drag it around.\n2. Set the Normal Map strength of the right material to 3.\n3. Set it to 0.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Textured materials, 2 \xB7 Walls (Brick)</color></size>"
